// question on import. The exception to format rule 3 and its reason stand in
// ../en.md, section 5. These lines carry what the header would have carried.
//
// Twelve graded questions, which is the number in the meta.yaml. The text
// before them is a description and is not graded.
// No text from a standard, neither in a question nor in an answer option.

$CATEGORY: iso-iec-27001

::Note ahead of the following questions::
The following questions test whether a requirement is found again at its clause
and whether it is told apart from a control in the annex. References are by
standard, clause and edition.

// 1

::Deselecting a requirement::
An organisation can deselect a requirement from clauses 4 to 10 of
ISO/IEC 27001\:2022 with a justification, the way a control from the annex can
be deselected.{FALSE
####False. Only a control is deselected, and the justification for that comes
out of the risk treatment. A requirement holds for every organisation running an
ISMS to this standard.}

// 2

::The clause the statement of applicability hangs off::
Which clause of ISO/IEC 27001\:2022 does the statement of applicability hang
off?{
=6.1.3 #Correct.
~4.3 #That is the scope.
~8.3 #That is carrying out the risk treatment in operation.
~9.3 #That is the management review.
####The statement is a result of the risk treatment and therefore stands with
the planning and not with the operation.}

// 3

::Competence and awareness::
An organisation fixes per role which ability is asked for a named task and how
it is evidenced. Which clause of ISO/IEC 27001\:2022 does that hang off?{
=7.2 #Correct.
~7.3 #That is about employees knowing their own role in the ISMS.
~7.4 #That is about communication.
~7.5 #That is about documented information, so about the record for it.
####7.2 asks about the ability for a task, 7.3 about knowing one's own role. A
briefing for everybody does not cover the first.}

// 4

::What a nonconformity is::
Which two cases are a nonconformity?{
~%50%A requirement from clauses 4 to 10 is not met. #Correct.
~%50%The organisation does not keep to something it laid down for itself.
#Correct.
~%-100%The organisation departs from a guidance document and meets the
requirement while doing so. #Certification is not against guidance.
~%-100%A control from the annex is not applied and the non-application is
justified. #That is a decision and not a finding.
####The measure is the requirement, and beside it whatever the organisation laid
down for itself. Guidance is not a measure.}

// 5

::Number of clauses carrying requirements::
How many clauses of ISO/IEC 27001\:2022 carry requirements that certification is
against?{#7:0
####They are clauses 4 to 10. The ones before them carry scope, references and
terms and are not checked.}

// 6

::Activity and clause::
Match each activity to the clause of ISO/IEC 27001\:2022 that asks for it.{
=Determining the scope -> 4.3
=Carrying out the risk assessment -> 6.1.2
=Carrying out the internal audit -> 9.2
=Taking a corrective action -> 10.2
####Four clauses, four steps. Whoever knows the rough division finds the place
without searching the whole standard.}

// 7

::A number that was not there before::
What does 6.3 of ISO/IEC 27001\:2022 stand for?{
=Changes to the management system that are carried out in a planned way.
#Correct.
~The information security objectives. #Those stand in 6.2.
~The risk treatment. #That stands in 6.1.3.
~The evaluation of performance. #That stands in clause 9.
####This clause exists only from the 2022 edition. Anyone with the previous
edition in mind looks for it in vain.}

// 8

::Departing from guidance::
An organisation implements a place differently from what ISO/IEC 27005 suggests
and meets the requirement from ISO/IEC 27001\:2022 while doing so. That is a
nonconformity.{FALSE
####False. The check is against the requirement. Guidance is no measure, and a
departure from it is no finding.}

// 9

::Gap, nonconformity and corrective action::
Nonconformity and corrective action stand in ISO/IEC 27001\:2022 in
{=10.2 ~10.1 ~9.2 ~8.1}.{####10.1 is continual improvement. In the previous
edition the two numbers stood the other way round, so an old checklist points at
the wrong one.}

// 10

::What has to stand for a control that is not applied::
What is the document called in which the decision to apply or not to apply a
control from the annex is recorded?{
=Statement of applicability
=the statement of applicability
=Statement of Applicability
####It hangs off 6.1.3 and shows for every number from the annex whether it is
applied and why. Without pointing back at the risk treatment the justification
is none.}

// 11

::A whole clause instead of a subclause::
Somebody says in the audit preparation\: "We train all staff once a year, that
covers clause 7." What stands out about the sentence?{
=It names a clause and no subclause, and the two requirements behind it are
different things. #Correct.
~It names too short an interval. #No interval is asked for.
~It names no certification body. #That does not belong in this question.
~It names no risk. #Clause 7 does not hang off a single risk.
####Behind the sentence stand 7.2 and 7.3, and the record for both hangs off
7.5. A briefing for everybody covers 7.3 and not 7.2.}

// 12

::Separating a requirement from a control::
A colleague suggests carrying the internal audit in the statement of
applicability as a control as well, so that everything stands in one place.
Write in two sentences what does not work about that.{
####Model answer. The internal audit is a requirement from 9.2 and not a control
from the annex, and a requirement is not decided about as to whether it is
applied. The statement of applicability carries the decisions about the
controls; entering a requirement there suggests it could be given up.}
